{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789849538,"nonce":"OBmW6XX31s2XPOmqp4Vk+2HIGr4=","title":"import toposort broke a cycle by emitting a file nothing depends on, before its own dependencies","message":"The cycle breaker picked the stuck file with the fewest outstanding dependencies. A user module with `using StringTools` depends on String and StringTools, which are in the stdlib cycle, but nothing depends on it, so it can never free anything -- yet it had 1 outstanding and won, and was typed before StringTools existed. Every static-extension call in it went `indirect` with an unresolved symbol (`str.unsafeCodeAt(p)` lowered to nothing, the local and everything reading it vanished). Now only a stuck file that some other stuck file depends on is a victim; the rest become ready once their dependencies land.","files":null}]}